                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "(Got this game courtesy of the developer's submission to SteadyGiveaways.  Thanks!)\n\n[h1]This is kinda' like that intro scene to that old show [i]3rd rock from the Sun[/i][/h1]\n\nSo, simply put?  You play Billiards using planets and asteroids to make all celestial objects (planets and asteroids) fly into the black holes.  When your asteroid enters the hole, the round is considered over, but you may still wait around a bit to make sure that a planet may still go into the blackhole late.  It'll still count.  Of course, you can also collect stars for completion and send space beings into the black hole too...like Superman, Space Invaders, Astronauts, and even Katamari...for some odd reason...\n\nThe graphics are minimalistic and the game feels like it was made using [i]GameMaker Studio[/i].  Not a bad thing, but it's not my preference of gaming.  This game also utilizes some physics involving gravitational fields both attracting and repelling.\n\nSo, is [i]Galactic Pocket Billiards[/i] worth your time?  Well, I personally didn't enjoy it, but to each his own.  You may end up enjoying it more than I did.  But for asking price ($4), I'd keep waiting for a sale to come by.  Preferred price for this game is a solid $1.\n\n3/10  Interesting, but gets boring.  Lost my attention about 30 minutes in...",
